  "user_request_original": "Design a 29-layer planar dielectric filter for 1550 nm LiDAR receiver. Incident medium is air. Substrate is Fused Silica. Materials are Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) in alternating sequence starting with Ta2O5 (Gao). Layer sequence: Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao). All 29 layer thicknesses are optimizable variables with bounds 50-400 nm. Solver uses coherent transfer-matrix method at normal incidence. Wavelength bands: 1400-1500 nm (suppress), 1550 nm (maximize transmittance), 1600-1700 nm (suppress). Objectives: maximize mean transmittance at 1550 nm, minimize mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm, minimize mean transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. Use L-BFGS optimizer with maximum step-size limit 0.015. Initialize cavity region layers 9-20 with refined grid sweep centered on previous optimal thicknesses from iteration 33.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 29-layer planar dielectric filter using alternating Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) layers on fused silica from air. Optimize all 29 layer thicknesses within 50–400 nm bounds using a coherent TMM at normal incidence. Maximize mean transmittance around 1550 nm while minimizing mean transmittance across 1400–1500 nm and 1600–1700 nm using L-BFGS optimization.",
